      "writtenOn": "2024-06-27T18:29:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the upstream, Linus said linux kernel expected the compiler to zero initialize left bytes with an empty initializer or a partial initializer. So the patch is unlikely to be accepted by upstream. Instead, clang upstream is happy to fix this bug, as in https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/78034. But waiting for a clang fix takes much more time, and needs a clang update.\n\nOn the other hand, the code in this CL probably is the only place that matters to android kernel. Because android kernel are built with -ftrivial-auto-var-init\u003dzero, so all local variables are zero initialized. For global variables and static variables in functions, I tried building 6.1 ACK with a check, there are three places having undefined fields, and the code here is the only place that matters. So I feel it\u0027s easier to just fix it.",
      "parentUuid": "14b20261_1710b119",
      "revId": "068164a16a17d56bc5ce2c0d81bcbe7749f0c8e3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
